{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum","id":1468722,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Essence (An attempt to add the Exalted to the Trinity Continuum)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-23T20:09:51-08:00","id":1468722,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Essence (An attempt to add the Exalted to the Trinity Continuum)","content":"This is a rather simple attempt by me to create the Exalted within the world and the system of the Trinity Continuum. Link <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pkruSUWxsGpB7IAYCYiewyU56vJOq35WwZoZj5zugcE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">HERE.</a><br /> <br /> I was inspired to make this homebrew thanks to the efforts of a number of different individuals as well as various Onyx Path properties. These include (of course) the 2nd Edition of the Trinity Continuum, the Essence version of Exalted, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar845_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"845\" data-vbnamecard=\"845\">Dragonmystic</a> 's &quot;Exalted Reincarnated&quot;, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> 's &quot;Fists of Flux,&quot; as well as Exalted vs. the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> In the current state (v. 0.1), I do not currently have any Charms, Caste/Aspect Powers or lore established. Almost all of the basic rules (outside of Caste/Aspect Powers and the Great Curse) are filled out, and I'd like to receive some feedback on what could be done better. My design intentions are as follows:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Exalts are powerful forces of nature, able to change the world for the better or the worse.</li> <li>Like Psions and Psiads, Exalts can access the 3rd Tier of Power (some naturally, others with effort) but have not yet evolved (or perhaps &quot;returned&quot;) to the level of strength seen in Quantum 6+ Novas.</li> <li>Charms are simple, singular and powerful. There are charms which every Exalt can use, and some which only a specific type can use (a la Exalted Essence).</li> <li>Terrestrial Exalts start better, Celestial Exalts finish better. However, both are still powerful and have their niches even at the very beginning or ending of campaigns.</li> <li>Essence is an easy-to-use, simple-to-retain, but difficult-to-regain resource a la Scion's Legend. While a portion is returned every so often, Exalts can also draw upon the strength of their bonds in order to regain points of Essence, at the cost of weakening those connections.</li> <li>Martial Arts will make their reappearance, but Sorcery will not, as I feel it intrudes in the niches carved out by Novas.</li> <li>Artifacts will also make their return alongside Evocations as Exalted &quot;Super-Science.&quot; Like some of the items discovered in the time of TC:Adventure!, Exalted Super-Science will have a much more mystical nature to them, such as flaming swords or magic carpets compared to the jetpacks and laser rifles of Novas and the Biotech of Psions.</li> </ol>Again, I'd love to hear any feedback you might have, and answer any questions that might come up. I'm looking towards filling out all of the Castes and Aspects next before moving on to the Great Curse and finally Charms. Thank you for your time and interest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T20:21:19-08:00","id":1468724,"title":"","content":"I know this guy who decided in his campaign that novas are the reincarnations of the Solar Exalted. But he was using Aberrant 1e and Exalted 2e at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T23:19:08-08:00","id":1468732,"title":"","content":"I am interested on how you plan on converting things for mass combat and combat in general.I was also going to use Exalted Essence to try to convert Exalted to Storypath rules but how to handle the two different damage types got me. That, and also Intimacies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T02:23:20-08:00","id":1468739,"title":"","content":"I like your ideas and would love to be able to help, but I am not that familiar to Exalted to help.<br /> <br /> My impressions are:<br /> While they are all Exalted, they are not the same in any way, Solar exalted are Nova like, while Dragonblooded are Talents at the best. So you may need to create a template for each of them instead of a general template that is adjusted to each of them.<br /> \u200bCharms can be build similarly to Techniques (from Fists of Flux), as it\u2019s Skill related, it is learned by studying (in opposition to just become available when you spend XP). To be fair I created much of the idea of Techniques from some old memories of Exalted charms, I was mainly too lazy to build all the charms, and instead created a system to create them as you neede (less work to me, more to the player, that will have to make his charms).<br /> On damage, you must embrace Storypath system, it means leas issues with one hit kills, but also less control in the qualities of charms amd weapons<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what AI have now. I must read your file with more calm and check my ExEss manuscript before I have more solid things to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-24-2021, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T18:37:48-08:00","id":1468801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1468732#post1468732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am interested on how you plan on converting things for mass combat and combat in general.I was also going to use Exalted Essence to try to convert Exalted to Storypath rules but how to handle the two different damage types got me. That, and also Intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intimacies are a bit easier if you just use the Bond system from Storypath and then make charms work with those instead, such as maybe having a charm that allows you to create &quot;regenerating&quot; bonds that &quot;heal&quot; on their own, what have you.<br /> <br /> Mass combat... I'll get to it eventually, though admittedly it's kind of on the backburner at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I like your ideas and would love to be able to help, but I am not that familiar to Exalted to help.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My impressions are:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While they are all Exalted, they are not the same in any way, Solar exalted are Nova like, while Dragonblooded are Talents at the best. So you may need to create a template for each of them instead of a general template that is adjusted to each of them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bCharms can be build similarly to Techniques (from Fists of Flux), as it\u2019s Skill related, it is learned by studying (in opposition to just become available when you spend XP). To be fair I created much of the idea of Techniques from some old memories of Exalted charms, I was mainly too lazy to build all the charms, and instead created a system to create them as you neede (less work to me, more to the player, that will have to make his charms).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On damage, you must embrace Storypath system, it means leas issues with one hit kills, but also less control in the qualities of charms amd weapons</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That\u2019s what AI have now. I must read your file with more calm and check my ExEss manuscript before I have more solid things to say.<br /> </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For the Nova/Talent comparison, I don't think comparing any Exalt to a standard Talent in terms of power level is a great idea. In Essence there's a lot of general &quot;prowess&quot; even among the Terrestrial Exalted, allowing them to still accomplish impressive feats, which leads me to believe that a Dragon-Blooded is at worst about on par with a Superior that then &quot;evolves&quot; into a Nova at a high enough Essence level. That's why I made the difference that I did between Celestial and Terrestrial: Celestial Exalts begin at Tier 3, meaning they have an easier time succeeding on rolls, but start at Essence 1, which means they're fairly strapped for MP. Terrestrials on the other hand start at Tier 2, so they don't do as well on rolls in general, but not only do they start at Essence 2 thanks to being an Exalt most/all of their lives (giving them more resource points and making their Excellencies even better at the start) but reaching Essence 3 and thus ascending to Tier 3 is only a mere 15 XP away. Maybe I should instead increase it to Essence 4 to give more of an edge to the Celestials, but that's something that can be dealt with later.<br /> <br /> My personal vision of Charms is that they work like Stalwart Gifts, providing a lot of power and having two different categories (General and Typical). I drew inspiration from DragonMystic's Exalted Reincarnated for the different &quot;tiers&quot; of charms, albeit 3 instead of 2, and combined that with Essence's Charm Modes for the idea of Leeways, exemptions that make certain charms easier to access depending on Exalt type. Being able to fly for example might be a 2nd Rank/Immortal Athletics Charm, for example, but Lunars can just shapeshift wings already, and so they can learn it at the start as a 1st Rank/Mortal charm. Solars unlike the other types do not naturally have any Leeways, being the most bread and butter Exalt type there is, but can opt into it with their Supernal Skill trait.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I will be using the Storypath combat system, I'm already working on how certain Anima Banner powers (Chosen of Battles and Endings, Dawn Caste, etc.) for example would function within it. Charms will be the same once I get started on those.<br /> <br /> ...Actually, now that I'm thinking about it, I'm kind of worried about Getimians, same with Exigents. The whole schtick of the former is &quot;Alternate Timelines,&quot; but that steps on the toes of Talents and other Flux users, while the latter's customization clashes with that of the Nova. In comparison, one could make the argument that a Lunar intrudes on Novas and their Mega-Attributes, but I think Lunars are sufficiently specific enough in their powers and intent that they'll be easy to set aside from the Novas, who are far more Build-a-Bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T19:45:45-08:00","id":1468805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1468801#post1468801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intimacies are a bit easier if you just use the Bond system from Storypath and then make charms work with those instead, such as maybe having a charm that allows you to create &quot;regenerating&quot; bonds that &quot;heal&quot; on their own, what have you.<br /> <br /> Mass combat... I'll get to it eventually, though admittedly it's kind of on the backburner at the moment.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but what about the difference between withering and decisive damage?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T20:07:31-08:00","id":1468808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1468805#post1468805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay but what about the difference between withering and decisive damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll have to be stripped out and replaced with Storypath combat, unfortunately. There's no reason to backport an entire combat system when we have something already available to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T03:01:21-08:00","id":1468822,"title":"","content":"That's exactly the issue that I had with it. That was where things broke down. The only thing I could think of was that, when it refers to Decisive damage to include Tags automatically to it or something. Or perhaps for Withering Combat to add Enhancement/Scale to a Decisive attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T11:08:51-08:00","id":1468855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1468822#post1468822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly the issue that I had with it. That was where things broke down. The only thing I could think of was that, when it refers to Decisive damage to include Tags automatically to it or something. Or perhaps for Withering Combat to add Enhancement/Scale to a Decisive attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, generally for Exalted I either drew from Essence or fan projects for inspiration. I don't there's any chance of converting the system here, so I'm thinking of just making up charm abilities wholesale and sticking familiar names on them. It's much easier than trying to work out how to apply one system to a completely different one, kind of like sticking a Base 10 equation into a Base 4 system. While it does mean needing to generate a lot more ideas for the charms would operate, it would also be less clunky than an attempt at a port.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T14:00:37-08:00","id":1468872,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head: Exalts come in two power levels, Celestial and Terrestrial. Solars (as well as their variants, the Abyssals and Internals), Lunars, Sidereals, and Alchemicals are comparable to Novas in power level, while Dragon-Blooded are comparable to Psions in power level. Exigents are, by definition, all over the board; they're literally intended to be a catch-all to let you make anything that doesn't fit the other types. I don't know enough about the Getimian or Liminal Exalted to say anything about their power levels. <br /> <br /> In terms of the <i>types</i> of Exalted, a lot of them are Talent-like: Solars/Abyssals/Infernals, Sidereals, and Dragon-Blooded have skill-based Charms that would work like what Talents and Assassins have, save only for the power level. Lunars and Alchemicals have Attribute-based powers that would be reasonable matches for Nova Mega-Edges. I'm pretty sure Liminals also fit the Attribute-based Mega-Edges approach (they're basically Frankenstein's monster); again, I'm not familiar enough with the Getimians to say; and again, the Exigents are catch-alls that could be either. <br /> <br /> In short, there are two power levels (Nova-like Celestials and Psion-like Terrestrials) and two power types (Gift-like skill-based Charms, and Mega-Edge-like attribute-based Charms). <br /> <br /> Solars are the most directly skill-based, though a number of their powers tend to have a sort of \u201cradiant energy\u201d theme: conjuring swords or arrows composed entirely of energy, for example. <br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are astrologers and martial artists. <br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods are \u201celement benders\u201d. <br /> <br /> Exigents, as stated above, are a catch-all. <br /> <br /> Abyssals are kind of like Solars, but with a death-aspects flavor to their powers. <br /> <br /> Infernals are also kind of like Solars, but with a demonic bent. <br /> <br /> Getimians are a sort of counterpoint to the Sidereals, people who were erased from the web of fate. <br /> <br /> Liminals are, as I said earlier, Frankenstein's monster. <br /> <br /> Alchemicals are mystical robots. <br /> <br /> That hits the main points of the Exalted setting. There are also a trio of inhuman races: Dragon Kings (supernaturally empowered dinosaurs), Mountain Folk (vaguely like dwarves), and Rakshasa (the Exalted version of the faerie folk). <br /> <br /> There are also some near-human variants, which don't have built-in powers; rather, they can Exalt the same way that regular humans can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-15-2021, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T18:05:59-08:00","id":1468878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1468855#post1468855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, generally for Exalted I either drew from Essence or fan projects for inspiration. I don't there's any chance of converting the system here, so I'm thinking of just making up charm abilities wholesale and sticking familiar names on them. It's much easier than trying to work out how to apply one system to a completely different one, kind of like sticking a Base 10 equation into a Base 4 system. While it does mean needing to generate a lot more ideas for the charms would operate, it would also be less clunky than an attempt at a port.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why I bring it up is that several Charms (some of them signature Charms of Exalted) boost/affect the two different types of damage. So that is why I ask.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T21:02:14-08:00","id":1468891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1468878#post1468878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why I bring it up is that several Charms (some of them signature Charms of Exalted) boost/affect the two different types of damage. So that is why I ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest, if perhaps not the most faithful conversion, would be to say &quot;If it adds to Withering, it's Enhancement. If it adds to Decisive, it's extra dice.&quot; That might seem backwards, but considering how Enhancement only works if you roll at least 1 success, having extra dice to roll is a hell of a thing, especially for the early game Terrestrials who are still rolling at target number 8.<br /> <br /> I'm still not fully satisfied with that idea however, and so once I get to combat I might just do something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T23:23:58-08:00","id":1468898,"title":"","content":"Well, I mentioned having Withering to add to Scale since, with Scale, you can buy the Inflict Damage Stunt multiple times and thus, allow you to be able to one shot someone...which is the point of the Exalted combat. You build up enough Withering so that, when you make a Decisive attack, you can severely hurt someone and possibly end them with one strong enough attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T14:37:15-08:00","id":1469128,"title":"","content":"So, an update on the project's progress: Currently it's at V0.2.0 after I added the Caste/Aspect Powers. I decided on giving each Caste/Aspect two powers, one passive and the other either dependent on having the Anima Banner active, or by spending 1 Essence. Solar, Abyssal and Infernal Castes share these categories (So all Night, Day and Nadir Castes have a power that activates when the Anima Banner is active, for example.) These abilities haven't been playtested yet of course, but I'm hoping that it will be refined to a better state in a quick fashion.<br /> <br /> While I don't have my notes with me at this moment, I do have everything regarding the Great Curse finished and ready to be transcribed onto the official document. One thing I've noticed in various editions about what to do regarding the Limit track is that they advise the player to roleplay as their Limit gets closer to the end, such as the character being more irritated or stressed, but nothing beyond that. Instead, I decided to create mechanics for this phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Every Exalt has a Limit Track with 10 spaces. Certain conditions can activate once per scene to give the Exalt 1 Limit (such as a Dragon-Blooded being in an environment devoid of their element, or a Lunar being restrained against their will.) Other conditions can once per session offer a reprieve, lowering limit by 1 (such as a Dragon-Blooded spending a scene surrounded by their element, or a Lunar breaking others free from confinement.) For the first 5 spaces, there are no additional effects. Past that, however...<br /> <br /> At Limit 6-7, the Exalt suffers from a condition called &quot;Limit Tension&quot; that impacts roleplaying (like a Sidereal experiencing bouts of paranoia, or an Abyssal generating deathly phenomena.) Terrestrial Exalted don't suffer from Limit Tension, but have another permanent condition that complicates their life (such as Liminals exposing their hideous appearance when their Anima Banner is active.)<br /> <br /> At Limit 8-9, the Exalt gains an additional condition called &quot;Limit Strain&quot; which has a drastic effect on the game (such as Sidereals infecting others nearby so that 2's also count for botches, or Abyssals becoming either too hideous or too beautiful and causing complications.)<br /> <br /> Finally, at Limit 10, the Exalt undergoes Limit Break and completely empties their track. For the rest of the scene, they go absolutely nuts (or cause others to go bonkers), causing major issues with the current situation (Sidereals for example cannot gain or spend momentum for the scene and neither can their allies. Abyssals become compelled to annihilate all life and it's very difficult to stop them from doing so.)<br /> <br /> Altogether, this system will hopefully make it so that the climb from 0 to 10 Limit will be more interesting and serve as an opportunity for more roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T21:12:25-08:00","id":1469224,"title":"","content":"Another quick update since I was able to get this out faster than I thought I would: I added all of the Great Curse mechanics to the document. In addition, I also finally added the rules for the Getimian Exalts and a few examples of Exigents: The Straw Maiden, the Metropolitan and the Mountaineer (who is totally not an excuse to backport the Mountain Folk into the rules I've created no, whatever could you be talking about?) The next update is going to take some time to put together, but I wanted to write up some general charms in the hopes of fine-tuning my ranking and Essence expenditure systems in the foreseeable future. If you have any questions or suggestions, once again feel free to do so!<br /> <br /> Oh, and for those wondering about lore, I'm going to be focusing on that element last, or at least once I have a few general and typical charms already completed. The idea I have running in my head currently is to embrace Trinity Continuum's &quot;tones&quot; and expand those out to different scenarios entirely: One where the world of Exalted is TC's very distant past, one where a region or even portal to Creation was opened up in the Adventure! era, and even one where the Exaltations were crafted by humans, likely even Novas a la the Modern Exalted shard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T21:01:09-08:00","id":1470498,"title":"","content":"So, another update. Remember how last time I said I would do lore last?<br /> <br /> Welp, I lied. Apparently charms were more difficult to write up than I thought, so I instead turned my creative efforts towards the &quot;background&quot; behind the Exalted and Essence (known sometimes here as &quot;Essential Energy,&quot; but generally just referred to by its smallest unit, Motes.) The list of origins I generated for the Exalted are non-exhaustive, feel free to come up with some stuff yourselves if you feel what I've added wasn't enough. What I'm looking to do is to embrace the spirit of the Trinity Continuum by having as many possible origins for the Exalted as possible, with most (if not all) of them being true. Hence why you could potentially have a Dragon-Blooded immigrant from Creation, the latest scion of a Sun God bloodline and someone enhanced with luck-altering nanomachines all still be &quot;Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> In addition, in my eyes Essence has a complicated relationship with the other types of Telluric Energy (Flux, Quantum and Noetic). On the one hand, unlike the other three Essence can genuinely do anything except for resurrection of the soul and time travel, there's nothing besides that which is beyond it's grasp. On the other hand, Essence has a very difficult time bonding together because the Telluric Energies are just so much smaller and intrusive, preventing most locales besides Creation from having any massive Essence-fueled structures or effects (No Sorcerous Workings, essentially). Thus, Essence is an omniapplicable energy source which cannot be used for large infrastructure or permanent transmutation because of the presence of competing forces. You could say it's my way of balancing it all out, but if you want to just disregard that bit of lore, feel free.<br /> <br /> As always, I welcome you to ask questions and post comments. I will try to focus on charms more now, but I think it's going to take me even longer than I suspected to even have the basic arrays done. Hopefully I'll have something done and ready by the time the new year rolls in, but I wouldn't hold my breath if I were you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T22:44:35-08:00","id":1470504,"title":"","content":"You might want to riff off of <b>Burn Legend</b>, one of the chapters in the Exalted 2e supplement <b>Shards of the Exalted Dream</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Set in the modern world, <b>Burn Legend</b> is a manga-inspired take on <b>Exalted</b>. In this shard, the Exalted do not exist as heroes chosen by the gods to act as their political and spiritual representatives. Rather, <b>Burn Legend</b> focuses on martial artists the world over, who are able to channel and use ki \u2014 the stream of life energy flowing through all things \u2014 to emphasize their martial prowess. Here, martial artists do not need the power of the Gods to exhibit extraordinary powers. There might come from arduous practice of ancient techniques honed over centuries, and the perfection of physical form. Emphasis lies on the heart of the fighter, the mentality he uses to get through the day, to train until his next big fight, and his raisins for doing so. The exalted do not exist as a quantifiable group of entities, but rather as an outgrowth of Martial arts. In this shard, the term \u201cExalted\u201d has no special meaning. Rather, the exalted are the strongest of those who can attune to the spirit energy around them, moving it with their ki. By this connection, and through unlocking ancient and terrible \u2014 sometimes otherworldly \u2014 martial arts, these humans take the next step, becoming greater and more powerful than any legend. It is said that in the moment a fighter reaches this peak, this nirvana, is Aura bursts into spirit flames. He steps into a world live with ancient spirits and new powers, and sees the ki of all things winding through the world and separating God's from men. Only then is the true path of battle open to him. </div>As I said, I'm thinking in terms of riffing off of this. That is, while <b>Burn Legend </b> as written is martial arts centric, what you're doing could and would extend well beyond that, with martial arts being but one manifestation of Essence \u2014 what <b>Burn Legend</b> calls ki. <br /> <br /> The factions described in <b>Burn Legend</b> are the Akuma, the Yamajin (Infernal Exalted), the Tennin (Sidereal Exalted), the Ryuujin (Dragon-Blooded), the Okami (Lunar Exalted), the Shinigami (Abyssal Exalted), and the Mugen (Solar Exalted). As written, <b>Burn Legend</b> has no place for Getimians, Liminals, Alchemicals, or Exigents; though as I said before, I'm recommending <b>Burn Legend</b> as a starting point; adding something like these Exalts wouldn't be hard. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I would recommend reading the entries that I just mentioned to get a sense of how the various kinds of Exalts can be reinterpreted in the context of the modern world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T23:06:44-08:00","id":1470506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1470504#post1470504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I would recommend reading the entries that I just mentioned to get a sense of how the various kinds of Exalts can be reinterpreted in the context of the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily I do own Shards of the Exalted Dream, so I'll check it out sometime soon. What I'm hoping is to have as many &quot;alternate histories&quot; as possible for the Exalted origins, to open up player choices. I've either outright drawn from canon or incorporated other gamelines or fan content together as potential worlds to draw from, with Creation (Exalted), the Mythical Past (Essentially Scion), Distant Future (Machineborn / Heaven's Reach). I think the most I'm willing to do myself would be 7, but more likely 5, after that people can just add whatever they want that's not covered. <br /> <br /> Also, you don't need to worry about different settings not having every type of Exalt. Each of the world entries thus far has types of Exalted that likely won't show up, such as Alchemicals for the Mythical Past, or Solaroids for the Distant Future. Obviously players can house-rule that as much as they want, but each world-line I guess you could call them is only going to provide so many types of Exalted, just as a lore thing rather than a limited player options thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T12:24:07-07:00","id":1487411,"title":"","content":"Very small update today, I just added some optional rules you can pick and choose from when playing in a low-Essence setting (such as Adventure! and Aberrant) or a high-Essence setting (such as Creation). This is mostly so that I can get back into the swing of things and start updating this project more regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T17:40:27-07:00","id":1508797,"title":"","content":"So, after so many months taking a break to give my mind space to breathe, I finally have the system for charms complete and actualized! For version 0.5, I have detailed charm families for Aim, Athletics, Close Combat, Integrity and Medicine, with the rest soon to be finished/worked on. I've also added some of the Exigent types present in the Exigents book as potential options. My plan for right now is to finish up all of the Universal Charms, and then start doing each Exalt type's charms one by one. For those curious, here are rules and some examples for what Universal Charms at least look like:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Charms</span><br /> <br /> Charms come in 2 general Categories, Universal and Specific. Universal Charms can be learned by any Exalt type, while Specific Charms can only be learned by 1 specific Exalt-type. They are organized into 3 levels of power: Mortal, Immortal and Exalted. Mortal Charms can be learned at any Essence level, and require around 1-2 dots in a Skill, or 2-3 dots in an Attribute (Universal Charms have both as potential requirements, depending on whether an Exalt focuses on Skills or Attributes). Immortal Charms require at least Essence 3, and 3-4 dots of either a Skill or an Attribute. Exalted Charms need Essence 5, and either 5 dots in a Skill, or 4-5 dots in an Attribute.<br /> <br /> Universal Charms are easier for certain types of Exalted to learn. Where most Exalted would have a tough time flying under their own power, Lunar Exalted can do so merely by growing wings. Infernal Exalted on the other hand easily run like the wind where others might struggle to sprint. These Exalted have a &quot;Leeway&quot;, which allows them to treat the Essence requirement as if it were 2 levels of lower. Thus, an Immortal Charm with an applicable leeway can be learned at Essence 1, and an Exalted Charm with the same could be learned at Essence 3. Solar and Abyssal Exalted do not have listed Leeways, and instead treat all Caste Skills as having an applicable Leeway due to their sheer talent.<br /> <br /> Examples:<ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trick Arrow Shot (Mortal)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Aim 2 or Dexterity 2</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalt can grapple targets using ranged weaponry out to (Essence/2) range bands away. Maintaining this grapple requires continually firing arrows at that target every turn. By spending 1 Mote, the Exalt can reduce the effective Size scale of a target for this purpose by (Essence) for 1 turn.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feather Foot Style (Mortal)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Athletics 2 or Dexterity 3</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Invest 1 Mote for the scene. The Exalt can walk across liquid surfaces without falling through, and can run up walls and ceilings, so long as they do not stop moving. They also reduce the damage rating of dangerous surfaces they walk across (such as lava) by (Essence).</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exalted Sword Flash (Exalted)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Close Combat 5 or Dexterity 5</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Leeway: Dragon-Blooded, Getimian</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Invest 2 Motes for the scene. For the duration, the Exalt\u2019s close combat attacks are treated as being indirect damage with a damage rating of (Power Scale + 1) which affect all enemies within short range. Durability Scale only reduces the damage on a 1-to-1 basis, and is treated as being (Essence/2, min 0) lower for this purpose.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit-Slaying Stance (Immortal)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Enigmas 3 or Cunning 3</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Leeway: All Celestial Exalted</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spend 1 Mote when taking out an entity in battle with lethal or greater damage. The entity is guaranteed to die, any power that would prevent their death or resurrect them is first rolled off with the target\u2019s Stamina + Integrity vs the Exalt\u2019s (Cunning or Resolve) + (Close Combat, Enigmas or Ranged Combat). The Exalt gains +1 Scale per difference in Tier between themselves and the target for the roll-off. On a success, the target can activate that power, otherwise they die.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ox-Body Technique (Mortal)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Integrity 1 or Stamina 2</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalt permanently gains 1 Hard Armor. In addition, increase the amount of Health levels provided at Stamina 3 and 5 by 1 each.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special: This charm can be purchased again at Essence 3 as an Immortal Charm requiring (Integrity 3 or Stamina 3), and again at Essence 5 as an Exalted Charm requiring (Integrity 5 or Stamina 4). Liminal and Lunar Exalted have leeway for these repurchases.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Divine Lifespan Blessing (Exalted)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: Medicine 5 or Intelligence 5</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Leeway: Getimian</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spend 2 Motes while treating a character. That character reduces their physical age by up to ((Essence - Target\u2019s Tier) x 10) years, to a minimum of 18. By investing an additional Mote, that character no longer ages so long as the Mote remains invested. Once it is withdrawn, the character rapidly ages to match their current physical age (after the initial reduction). Every time this charm is used again on the same character by any Exalt, increase the initial cost by 1 Mote. Exalted of the same Essence or greater than the Exalt cannot benefit from this charm due to their greater metaphysical weight, and Sidereal Exalted cannot benefit at all. Abyssal Exalted receive no benefit as they disregard aging already.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Admittedly, I did draw on Exalted Essence a lot for inspiration here, but I tried to have some original things as well.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T23:17:23-07:00","id":1508843,"title":"","content":"Apologies for posting again so soon, but Inspiration struck me as it were, and I busted out some Super-Science rules in about an hour. Here's a preview for those curious:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exalted Crafting</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalted replace the Super-Science table used in the TC Core Rulebook with the following below. By default, only items of Ranks 1-5 can be constructed, once an Exalt has reached Essence 6 or higher, they unlock 1 Rank per dot of Essence above 5. Mental Scale is an exception: For every point of Mental Scale above 1 the Exalt possesses, they can either treat the Rank of an item they are working on as 1 lower for the purposes of time and materials, OR unlock the next-highest Rank of project.</span></span><br /> \u200b <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Rank</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Max Enhance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Maximum Edge Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Max Evo Level</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Max Tag</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Time Between</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 dot of M/P/S Edge</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">None</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Session</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 dots of M/P/S Edges</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">None</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2 Sessions</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Up to 5 dots of Mental, Physical or Social Edges OR up to 3 dots of Style Edges OR 1 Defined Evocation</span></span>\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 Sessions</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Up to 9 dots; No more than 2 Evocations (Loose Evocations cost 2 dots, Defined Evocations cost 3 dots)</span></span>\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Story Arc</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Up to 11 dots; No more than 3 Evocations</span></span>\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2 Story Arcs</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Up to 15 dots; At least 1 Evocation and no more than 5.</span></span>\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Immortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 Story Arcs</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Up to 20 dots; At least 1 Evocation and no more than 7.</span></span>\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Immortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Chronicle</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Up to 25 dots; At least 2 Evocations and no more than 9.</span></span>\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Exalted</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2 Chronicles</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Up to 30 dots; At least 3 Evocations and no more than 11.</span></span>\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Exalted</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 Chronicles</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations are custom Charms which fits the item\u2019s materials, purpose and legend. Uniquely among Super-Science items, Exalted \u201cArtifacts\u201d as they are known have a degree of customization for their user. They can create wildly different power sets depending on the user, while still holding true to their usual themes. These \u201cLoose\u201d Evocations require the user to purchase them with XP as if they were Charms of the appropriate level, but are otherwise customizable to match the user, so long as it still suits the item\u2019s themes. However, they cannot be utilized by anyone other than Essence wielders.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, \u201cDefined\u201d Evocations must be defined by the creator at the moment of creation, at least in terms of utility, but do not need to be learned by the user to wield. They must still fit the item\u2019s themes. In addition, baselines and other characters who wield Artifacts can use these Defined Evocations themselves, substituting Momentum, Inspiration, Quantum Points, Psi Points or even Injury Conditions for Essence.</span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An Artifact can have at most half of their Evocations be Defined (rounded up). At least half of their Loose Evocations (rounded up) must be Mortal Level. Rank 6+ Artifacts are always storied items, just by their construction if not their deeds. Treat them as having (Rank - 5) dots of the Fame Edge. Rank 9 Artifacts have the Living Legend Enhanced Edge instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalted in Creation define Artifacts as being of 3 levels: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Talismans</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, which most mortal sorcerers can content themselves with creating, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Lesser Wonders</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, which most so-called Artifacts truly are, and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>True Artifacts</i>, which have legendary backgrounds all on their own. These roughly correspond to Ranks 1-2, 3-5 and 6-9. They notably do NOT line up with the general Super-Science categories and are mostly descriptive. Treat \u201cAdvanced Science\u201d as a 1-dot Edge granting +1 Scale, \u201cInspired Science\u201d as a 3-dot Edge granting +2 Scale instead, and \u201cPowered Science\u201d as a 5-dot Edge granting +3 Scale instead, each of which requires the prior. The Scale provided this way only affects 1 type of Scale, multiple varieties require multiple purchases.</span></span>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T19:30:27-07:00","id":1509676,"title":"","content":"Back again with a new update, this time regarding Martial Arts, and with it comes a question that will be presented later. I also have the &quot;basics&quot; of Spirits taken care of, though that will likely need to be adjusted with time as well.<br /> <br /> Starting with the latter, Spirits are sentient Essence constructs which only function effectively in High-Essence Environments (essentially, Creation, rather than Aeon or TC:Core's setting). Outside of such environments, Spirits must either spend 1 Mote or suffer 1 Aggravated Injury Condition each scene as their body cannibalizes its internal power structure for fuel. This can be resolved through the use of powers or Super-Science, but is otherwise unavoidable.<br /> <br /> Most spirits, with the exception of elementals, are &quot;dematerialized characters&quot;. Dematerialized characters are entities which do not have a material presence in reality, such as, again, most spirits, Psions using astral projection, Novas using Immaterial Phasing, or other such entities. Dematerialized characters cannot normally be interacted with physically, though they can psychically unless stated otherwise. The Exalted however are specialists in dealing with dematerialized characters: Spirit-Cutting Glance (which requires either Enigma 1 or Cunning 2) allows them to see, touch and attack such entities, Spirit-Grounding Shout makes them material and affected by heavy gravity, Spirit-Slaying Stance can permanently destroy them and Spirit-Repelling Diagram allows the Exalt to create barriers which stop their entry. These and more are all universal charms the Exalted host have access to, with some like Lunars and Liminals taking this expertise to greater heights.<br /> <hr /><br /> And now, we get to Martial Arts. Martial Arts, or rather Mystic Martial Arts, is the privilege and specialty of the Exalted. These styles of combat call upon spiritual themes in order to extract heightened performance. While only the Exalted can Master such arts, they CAN be taught to non-Exalted, albeit very inefficiently. How this is done is as follows:<br /> <br /> The Exalted naturally have access to Martial Arts so long as they have at least 1 dot in Close Combat. After that, they can purchase Martial Arts Charms. MA Charms have 3 requirements, of which only 2 are needed to actually learn: A minimum rating in Close Combat, a minimum rating in a style-chosen Attribute, and a minimum rating in some other Skill. Technically speaking, you don't even need Close Combat beyond the first dot to access these arts: A Righteous Devil has little use for hand-to-hand combat when they can just shoot everything with Ranged Combat and judge their targets with Resolve. You can also substitute the selected Attribute and Skill for the normal stats when making unarmed attacks, or with attacks that have the right weapon tags.<br /> <br /> Just like Universal Charms, certain styles also have Leeways for a given Exalt type. If the Exalt matches the Leeway, they treat the Essence Requirement of charms as being 2 lower. The Immaculate Dragon Styles for example are uniquely suited to the Dragon-Blooded, and Solars are greatly suited towards Righteous Devil. Sidereals are the only Exalt type to have a universal Leeway for Martial Arts, outside of Solars and Abyssals with the right Caste Skills.<br /> <br /> Every MA Charm also has a Mastery benefit, which either enhances the original effect or provides an alternative use. Exalted that have all 3 requirements fulfilled unlock this Mastery effect. Alternatively, having a Leeway automatically unlocks it as well. In either case, Mastery of a Martial Arts Charm is necessary in order to teach the style to non-Exalted.<br /> <br /> Non-Exalted must purchase some form of &quot;initiation&quot; into the Martial Arts to use them. Spirits just have to buy a certain charm once (or twice to unlock Mastery effects). Those who cannot use Essence must employ more roundabout means, and also suffer a +1 dot requirement to all MA Charms (max Attribute rating 6, max Skill rating 5). These are as follows:<ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Talents and other Inspired must learn the Close Combat Skill Gift \u201cChakra Alignment\u201d which requires Close Combat 2 or more. Talents gain Mastery by repurchasing Charms again at 1 level higher (Mortal -&gt; Immortal -&gt; Exalted), which requires additional instruction and all 3 traits fulfilled. They treat the required Essence as equivalent to (Inspiration/2, rounded down), and 1/2 points of Inspiration equals 1 invested/spent Mote.</span></span>\u200b</li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Psiads and Psions must develop a special 1-dot Mode called &quot;Motonics&quot;, which uses their least favored XP Cost. They unlock the Mastery effect by purchasing the 2nd-dot of Motonics and having the correct traits. They treat their (Psi Rating - 1) as equivalent to Essence, and 2/3 Psi Points equals 1 invested/spent Mote.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Novas must learn a special Mega-Edge called \u201cMega-Enlightenment\u201d. They treat their Quantum Rating as equivalent to Essence, and can add their Mega-Attribute dots to their Attribute dots to meet the requirements. They unlock Mastery by purchasing the Mega-Edge a 2nd time, and 3/5 Quantum Points equals 1 invested/spent Mote.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Baselines by default cannot learn Martial Arts. However, they can pay 15 XP to learn \u201cChakra Alignment\u201d, which provides sufficient Inspiration to immediately transform them into a Talent. After that, they use the same rules as above.</span></span></li> </ul>There's also Sidereal Martial Arts, but I'm still working through that at the moment.<br /> <br /> Now, for the question I mentioned earlier. I forgot until I was finished with this whole ruleset for Martial Arts that Style Edges are a thing. Since those do represent mortal knowledge of Martial Arts, I was wondering: Should I scrap the special powers for initiating into Martial Arts in favor of a Style Edge that does the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T01:48:47-07:00","id":1509698,"title":"","content":"I personally would go in that direction (Style edges). I am actually writing some style edges that combined (some give access to the edges some have prerequisites in the styles) would work as Wuxia and mystical martial arts (moving away from Fists of Flux a bit but not removing it from the game.<br /> <br /> For example one of my ideas is picking a regular talent gift (On the Head of a Pin, for example) and adding an style edge that allow you to do some special maneuvers and stunts (in the example, some aerial combat, but not really fly). Other examples are Know Thine Enemy gift, that could convince the character to do things other than attacking, or Doctor of Destruction to do some nerve puncture, paralyzing or stunning the target mid combat.<br /> <br /> By the way, I really like the way it\u2019s going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T16:04:54-07:00","id":1509792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1509698#post1509698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would go in that direction (Style edges). I am actually writing some style edges that combined (some give access to the edges some have prerequisites in the styles) would work as Wuxia and mystical martial arts (moving away from Fists of Flux a bit but not removing it from the game.<br /> <br /> For example one of my ideas is picking a regular talent gift (On the Head of a Pin, for example) and adding an style edge that allow you to do some special maneuvers and stunts (in the example, some aerial combat, but not really fly). Other examples are Know Thine Enemy gift, that could convince the character to do things other than attacking, or Doctor of Destruction to do some nerve puncture, paralyzing or stunning the target mid combat.<br /> <br /> By the way, I really like the way it\u2019s going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm glad to hear you're enjoying it. Obviously, I'm still trying to figure out how exactly Martial Arts would fit with the already established Style Edges. There's three paths I can think of, though let me know if you have any better ideas:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Style Edges as INITIATION for Mystic Martial Arts. Basically, for non-Exalted, they would need to invest in a certain Style Edge (or likely 1 of several, depending on which one) in order to access a given MA Style. For example, 3 dots in Precise Martial Arts could unlock Snake Style, 3 dots in Forceful Martial Arts could unlock Tiger, 3 dots in Free Running for Falcon, etc.</li> <li>Style Edges AS the Martial Art. Instead of doing charms altogether, each MA Style is a Style Edge that anyone can learn, though Exalted might have easier access.</li> <li>As above, but Sidereal Martial Arts are still Charms. Basically, &quot;normal&quot; Martial Arts are just powerful Style Edges, but Sidereal Martial Arts are so esoteric that they must be learned via charms (and can only be learned by the Exalted).</li> </ol>In other news, I also added some new potential origins for the Exalted. One admittedly is just Promethean with the serial numbers filed off, while the other is kind of &quot;Avatar the Last Airbender meets Evil Dead,&quot; the third is a Space Opera featuring star-aligned Solars, black hole-created Abyssals, and mantis-people Sidereals, because I think its cool. If I'm doing all of these alternate origins for the Exalted, I think I should be clear for at least one alien Exalt what with there being alien Noetic and Quantum users, right? Which leads into the last one I added, which is essentially a &quot;Earth with no humans&quot; alternate timeline where Gaia rose up and made animal-originating Lunars. Does that go against the rules established in Exalted proper? Yeah. Is it cool? I think it could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T16:58:34-07:00","id":1510289,"title":"","content":"New Update (v.0.7.5, close to completion): Sorcery<br /> <br /> Yes, I did say before that I had no intentions of adding sorcery into the mix. That was before I realized that the Super-Science rules could easily be adapted to Workings as well. So, here are my rules for Sorcery thus far. Note that I have no idea what to do with spells thus far and am still trying to come up with something. I could do the usual learned formulas, or maybe I could do something like power stunts for Novas. Regardless, I DO have rules for Sorcery in general as well as workings.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sorcery</span><br /> <br /> Sorcery is the art of altering reality to fit the will-worker's desire. It is divided into 3 Circles of Proficiency (First, Second, Third) and 3 Categories of specialization (Miraculous, Necromantic and Prophetic). The 3 categories correlate to standard-Sorcery, Necromancy and Astrology in Exalted proper (see the document for more details). To begin using Sorcery, one must purchase the Sorcerous Initiation Charm (Mortal), and then later repurchase it as an Immortal and Exalted Charm for the 2nd and 3rd initiations. These Initiation charms have no Leeways, not even for Solars or Abyssals.<br /> <br /> The first time the Exalt is initiated, they unlock the 1st Circle of a given category corresponding to their Exalt Type (Solars unlock the First Circle of Miraculous Sorcery, and Sidereals First Circle Prophetic Sorcery). When they are initiated a second time, they improve their first category to Second Circle, and unlock a second category of their choice to First Circle. The third time, the first category reaches Third Circle, the second Second Circle, the third First Circle.<br /> <br /> However, not all Exalted can reach the Third Circle for any given category. Solars and Infernals can do so for Miraculous Sorcery, Abyssals for Necromantic Sorcery and Sidereals for Prophetic Sorcery. Everyone else, when they initiate for the third time, instead treat the Essence Density of the area they are in as 1 level higher for the purposes of Sorcery (thus making them more efficient at the cost of potential). The non-Third Circle types also have two choices for their primary category instead of being stuck with one.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Exalt Type</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Primary Category</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Max Circle Rating</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Solar</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Miraculous</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Third</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dragon-Blooded</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Miraculous/Necromantic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Second</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lunar</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Miraculous/Necromantic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Second</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sidereal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Prophetic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Third</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Abyssal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Necromantic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Third</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Infernal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Miraculous</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Third</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Alchemical</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Miraculous/Prophetic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Second</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Liminal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Necromantic/Prophetic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Second</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Getimian</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Necromantic/Prophetic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Second</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerous Workings work just like Super-Science projects. They are different from artifacts in that they alter reality in order to achieve a given outcome. Due to their heavy reliance on Essence Density, Sorcerous Workings are more limited in dimensions outside of Creation. The less Essence there is, the less powerful a Working can be and the shorter it's lifespan. A Working with a \u201cForever\u201d Duration lasts forever: The Exalt does not need to supply Essence to sustain it, and it cannot be undone except with another Working (or similar effort) to alter it back into how it used to be. \u201cContinuous (Year)\u201d means that the Working lasts for (Essence) years, and after that dissipates unless the Exalt spends (Circle Used) Motes to extend its duration by another year. Maintained means that the Exalt must maintain the initial Mote investment, otherwise the Working fades immediately.</span></span>\u200b<br /> \u200b <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Essence Density</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Example Location</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Maximum Working Circle</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Maximum Working Rank</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Duration</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">High</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Creation</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Third</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Forever</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Medium</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">TC - Core</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Second</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Continuous (Year)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Low</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">TC - Aberrant</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">First</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Maintained</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To begin a Working, the Exalt must designate the Rank of the project, which is limited by their initiated Circle and Essence Density: First Circle for Rank 1-3, Second Circle for Rank 4-6, Third Circle for Rank 6-9. Then, they must Invest Motes equal to the corresponding Circle. After that, things work as they would for a Super-Science project. Flaws work the same as with Super-Science, as do Crafting Stunts.</span></span>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One important thing to note is that Ranks within each Circle are not inherently more \u201cpowerful\u201d than another. Rather, the higher a Working\u2019s Rank within a given Circle, the more accurate it becomes to their desires. A Rank 1 and Rank 2 Working can both bless a wheat field to become immune to disease, but the Rank 2 Working does so by fortifying their genetic code as the Sorcerer wished, while the Rank 1 Working did so by creating symbiotic fungi that protect the wheat at the cost of making it taste weird. Both accomplished the task, but the Rank 2 Working did so to specification. Rank 3/6/9 Workings can also include contingencies, adapting the Working to changing circumstances.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Specification Levels:</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">None: There is no focus as to how the goal is accomplished, just that it is.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Contained: The Working is accomplished through some general method: A \u201cbiological\u201d method differs wildly from an \u201cengineering\u201d method. Rank 1/4/7</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Focused: The Working is performed exactly as the Sorcerer desires. Rank 2/5/8</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adapting: The Working can adapt to changing circumstances beyond its normal parameters, to a point. Rank 3/6/9</span></span></li> </ol>\u200b <hr /><br /> So yeah, let me know what you all think. I'm still working on how spells are going to work (not to mention Martial Arts, still haven't decided on something yet), so any advice helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T01:17:49-07:00","id":1510333,"title":"","content":"I forget: do the Super-Science rules have anything in them for jury-rigging? If so, then in the same way that a Working is a Super-Science project that alters reality instead of making an artifact, casting a spell could perhaps be treated as \u201cjury-rigging reality\u201d.<br /> <br /> EDIT: yep; there it is, on pages 98 and 99. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-01-2023, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T02:58:18-07:00","id":1510340,"title":"","content":"On Martial Arts, because I still have to reread your previous post properly, but from your 3 options, I would go with 1\u2026 ish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Style Edges as INITIATION for Mystic Martial Arts. Basically, for non-Exalted, they would need to invest in a certain Style Edge (or likely 1 of several, depending on which one) in order to access a given MA Style. For example, 3 dots in Precise Martial Arts could unlock Snake Style, 3 dots in Forceful Martial Arts could unlock Tiger, 3 dots in Free Running for Falcon, etc.</li> <li>Style Edges AS the Martial Art. Instead of doing charms altogether, each MA Style is a Style Edge that anyone can learn, though Exalted might have easier access.</li> <li>As above, but Sidereal Martial Arts are still Charms. Basically, &quot;normal&quot; Martial Arts are just powerful Style Edges, but Sidereal Martial Arts are so esoteric that they must be learned via charms (and can only be learned by the Exalted).</li> </ol>\u200b </div> </div> </div>You can have the styles we already have, and more restricted styles for more advanced martial arts and the real powers are Charms. <br /> <br /> So you have the first level for mundane martial arts, a second level for the Snake Style and Tiger Style, still on reach of mortals but exalted being the true focus, and a third level that is made of charms, that only exalted.<br /> <br /> I am not completely aware of the details that goes from one kind of Exalted to the other, so you may need to have Sideral Martial Arts with extra style edges that only them can have, but I would make them into charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T21:53:08-07:00","id":1510559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1510333#post1510333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget: do the Super-Science rules have anything in them for jury-rigging? If so, then in the same way that a Working is a Super-Science project that alters reality instead of making an artifact, casting a spell could perhaps be treated as \u201cjury-rigging reality\u201d.<br /> <br /> EDIT: yep; there it is, on pages 98 and 99. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, here's what I've got so far:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spells in TC: Essence are more like pseudo-Workings than the formulated powers shown in Exalted proper. They are effectively Jury-Rigged projects, which require a number of completed milestones equal to (Working Rank / 2, rounded down) + 1. A given spell can do anything a Working of the same circle can do, but with less focus and duration: Treat the specificity of a spell as 1 level lower than that of an equivalent Working (min: None), and treat its duration as 1 level lower per the Essence Density chart (min: Concentration). In addition, all Spells require twice their Rank in Flaws, just as jury-rigged projects do. The most common Flaw used is One-Time Use, but others can also be applied instead for longer-lasting spells.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition, there are several other Flaws specifically intended for Spells, as shown below:</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Big Boom (oooo)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires: One-Time Use</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalt\u2019s spell only lasts a single turn. This is commonly used for powerful offensive magic, but could also be done for a potent healing effect or a teleport.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Different Wavelengths (o)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spell only affects dematerialized characters, it does not affect any material entity.</span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Just a Touch (o - oo)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalt\u2019s spell requires them to be within close range of the target in order to work. At 2 dots, they must physically touch the target to accomplish their goal. The Exalt is always considered to be within touch range for the purposes of this charm.</span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sustenance (ooo - ooooo)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spell, if beneficial, can only benefit Tier 2 or higher characters as their internal energies provide energy for the spell\u2019s effects. At 5 dots, it only affects Tier 2+ characters who use Essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sympathy (oo+)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order for the spell to affect the target, the Exalt must have one item or piece of evidence tied to the target. For every dot after the first two, add an additional item to this requirement. Each item must be distinctly different from each other (blood and hair can be two separate items, but not strips of cloth from the same shirt.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trace Evidence (o - ooooo)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After the spell is finished, investigators gain (Dot Rating) enhancement to figure out what spell was cast, when it was cast and who casted it.</span></span><br /> <hr />More can be found in the doc itself. Let me know what you think. As for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> 's suggestion, I'll try and create an example that fits your suggestion, when I have the time. As far as I understand it, you are suggesting a 3-step pyramid:<br /> <br /> 1. Normal Style Edges, like those already present in the TC: Core book, which anyone can learn.<br /> 2. Powered Style Edges for Snake Style and others of that level, which Tier 2+ characters can learn and benefit from.<br /> 3. Sidereal Martial Arts which take the form of charms and which only Exalted can learn.<br /> <br /> Is this correct?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T02:52:34-07:00","id":1510580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468722-trinity-continuum-essence-an-attempt-to-add-the-exalted-to-the-trinity-continuum?p=1510559#post1510559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More can be found in the doc itself. Let me know what you think. As for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> 's suggestion, I'll try and create an example that fits your suggestion, when I have the time. As far as I understand it, you are suggesting a 3-step pyramid:<br /> <br /> 1. Normal Style Edges, like those already present in the TC: Core book, which anyone can learn.<br /> 2. Powered Style Edges for Snake Style and others of that level, which Tier 2+ characters can learn and benefit from.<br /> 3. Sidereal Martial Arts which take the form of charms and which only Exalted can learn.<br /> <br /> Is this correct?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thats the idea I am working on at least. Well, my idea is not related to Sideral Martial Arts, and my idea is strictly to Talents, but thats what I am going with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T16:51:19-07:00","id":1510734,"title":"","content":"Alright! I have put the pedal to the medal before taking a small personal vacation, and have come up with the revised ruleset and examples of Martial Arts: <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While anyone can learn and practice martial arts, the Exalted are the greatest martial artists in the cosmos. No entity or species (save maybe the Celestial Incarnae and the greatest of demons) can ever exceed them in prowess in this regard. They are also the greatest instructors in martial arts, and this can be seen in their creation of several styles which non-Exalted can use, which nonetheless are superior to the normal fare. Still, there are some styles, referred to as the Lotus (or in the First Age, the \u201cSidereal\u201d) Styles, which only the Exalted can learn, barring one or two exceptions. In this section, we will cover both examples.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are 3 effective tiers of martial arts, which roughly correspond to character Tiers.</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Standard Style Edges,</u> like Precise Martial Arts (see TC: Core). These can be learned by anyone, even baselines, in order to gain the benefits. They represent the basic training in martial arts like blocking and practicing strikes. Tier 2 or higher characters must have fully mastered a given Style Edge in order to advance, but the Exalt can skip this stage if they desire. Any points invested are purely for the benefits of the Edge.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Mystic Martial Arts</u> are special Style Edges which can only be learned by Tier 2+ characters. They represent the \u201cnormal\u201d Martial Arts of Exalted proper, such as Snake or Tiger Style. Exalted can learn these styles with no requirements, and indeed must master at least 1 Mystic Style in order to advance. Other Tier 2+ characters can only learn them by mastering a Standard Style, and cannot advance any further barring Storyguide fiat.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Lotus Martial Arts</u> are not Style Edges, but instead a line of charms from Mortal to Exalted. To begin learning these Charms, the Exalted must be Tier 3, and must have a Mystic Style fully mastered which corresponds to the Lotus Style they are attempting to learn. Lotus Martial Arts are purchased in a vague order: Before you purchase the Immortal level charms, you must first purchase all of the Mortal level charms, and the same with the Exalted level charms. Unlike standard charms, Mortal level charms require Essence 3, Immortal Essence 5 and Exalted Essence 7 (which is likely impossible outside of Creation). Leeways exist for entire styles, which reduce the Essence requirement of every charm in that style by 2 points. Sidereal and Getimian Exalted have a universal leeway for Lotus Martial Arts. Leeways are important for another reason: Only someone with a Leeway who has fully mastered a Lotus Martial Art can instruct others in its ways.</span></span></li> </ol><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Standard Styles</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gunslinger (o to ooo)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Cunning 3, Aim 2 and an appropriate Path</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rather than merely focusing on precision, the character also tries their best to fire at a target as quickly as possible without sacrificing efficacy. Your character cannot use these maneuvers with shotguns and other projectile launchers that only fire once before needing to reload.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(o) Steady Hand:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Increase the amount of successes needed to disarm the character\u2019s gun by (Gunslinger).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>(oo) Quick Draw:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While wielding a pistol or other small gun in one hand, treat the character as having Speed Scale 2 for the purposes of initiative. With all other applicable weapons, gain 1e for initiative instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>(ooo) Gun Fu:</b> The character can fire applicable guns in close range with only +1 Difficulty.</span></span>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mystic Styles</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mystic Styles are structured as follows:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(o) The prerequisite style gains a small permanent bonus. Exalted gain an additional benefit they must spend or invest Motes for. This way, both Exalted and non-Exalted characters gain a benefit for investing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(oo) Some sort of activateable ability. Exalted can use Essence to do it reflexively, while other characters can take a simple action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(ooo) The Form of the style. A given character can only be in one Martial Arts form at a time, whether that be Mystic or Lotus Martial Arts. Entering the form takes an action, or investing 1 Mote for Exalted. It lasts for the scene, or until switched to another form. While in the form, the character gains several passive benefits which fit with the style\u2019s overall themes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(oooo) As with the 2 dot option, generally more powerful.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(ooooo) The capstone of the style, it can be an enhancement for the Form or a powerful technique akin to the 2 and 4 dot benefits.</span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Righteous Devil Style (o to ooooo)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Requires:</b> Gunslinger ooo OR Exalted; Aim ooo, Resolve ooo</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Righteous Devil Style is the art of the gunslinger and the firebrand, the lone figure that pursues justice for crimes committed. Part of the instruction in this style involves morality, either in some defined code or a loose philosophy, but it always involves some form of ethics. Righteous Devil Style techniques can be used with pistols, rifles and weapons with the Incendiary tag.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>(o) Kiss of Sun Concentration:</b> Weapons with the Incendiary tag qualify for the benefits of Gunslinger, no matter their size. Exalted wielding weapons with this tag can spend 1e to grant their weapon the Explosive (Ranged) tag for the turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>(ooo) Righteous Devil Form:</b> Take a simple action or invest 1 Mote for the scene. When this Form is activated, the character reflexively rolls (Presence + Persuasion) to create an atmosphere of fear, shame, guilt or remorse. They reduce the Difficulty to do so by 1 per Tier above the highest Tiered enemy. Enemies within the scene suffer a Difficulty increase to all rolls to retreat or hide equal to the generated Atmosphere level. Finally, guns wielded by the character gain the Melee tag, allowing them to be used with the Close Combat skill in close range.</span></span>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>(ooooo) Caress of 1000 Hells:</b> After spending a simple action and taking no other actions that turn (or by spending 2 motes with a simple action), the character can on their next turn roll Presence + (Aim or Persuasion) against a Difficulty of the target\u2019s Resolve. On a success, the target faces a choice: They can either suffer a Persistent Injury Condition in their worst available Injury box, or the target must immediately form a Bond of remorse towards an individual or group which they have wronged. They are compelled to do something to make up for this crime, as if the Exalt had successfully persuaded them to do so.</span></span>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lotus Styles</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most Lotus Styles have origins within Creation, and thus are more difficult to find a teacher for outside of its boundaries. This doesn\u2019t mean that it's impossible, simply that the Exalt might need to find some other, more esoteric means of instruction like an enchanted technique manual.</span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Requires:</b> ANY Mystic Style ooooo; Culture oo, Science oo</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Leeway:</b> All Exalted</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Origin:</b> Creation</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style is a unique creation, in that it is designed from the ground up to be easy to access by non-Sidereals. Originally, it was thought that its connection to 4 of the 5 Magical Materials is what allowed for its universal ease. However, this was soon proven wrong when the Liminal Exalted, which favored the last remaining material \u201csoulsteel,\u201d were able to learn the style themselves. The emerging Abyssal Exalted, also able to wield it, suggested that the magical materials were not the true connection point. New theories suggest it may be a result of the Charm \u201cWays of Exaltation,\u201d but even this is hypothetical at best.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regardless, Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style is easy to learn and offers many applications outside of combat. The toolbelt of options it provides means that over half of the Sidereals employed by the Bureau of Destiny know at least 1 charm in the style.</span></span><br /> \u200b<ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">God Ways (Mortal)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Invest 1 Mote. While active, the Exalt dematerializes and possesses an object within close range, up to Size Scale 2. By default, the Exalt cannot move or act outwardly while possessing an object, but by spending 2 Motes, they can regain mobility and act for a scene using their normal Scale - 1 (except for Size or Mental Scale). Destroying the object does not harm the Exalt and merely exorcizes them, unless magic that targets dematerialized characters is used.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Four Magical Materials Form (Immortal)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Invest 3 Motes for the scene. For the duration, the Exalt treats their body as if it were an Artifact of Rank (Essence). They automatically gain the \u201cAdvanced Science (Power)\u201d tag, and can assign the remaining dots for more Edges. They can also use these dots to develop Evocations for this Form as if they were an Artifact. In addition, they become immune to all effects that would immobilize or cripple the Exalt\u2019s limbs. Finally, the Exalt gains the ability to use Powered Super Science items for other energy sources (Flux, Noetic, Quantum or Aether).</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form (Exalted)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Charm is not a true Form charm, so much as it is a culmination in the concept of \u201cForms.\u201d When learned, the Exalt gains the ability to maintain 2 Martial Arts Forms at once. By investing an additional 2 motes, the Exalt can maintain a third Form on top of this, and reduces the mote cost of Mystic Forms and this style\u2019s Forms by 1 each (min 0).</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><hr /><br /> The Styles shown here are fully completed in the document. I'll be working on more once I get back from my break. If you have any questions, let me know!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T17:16:46-07:00","id":1511418,"title":"","content":"Making more progress with the doc. I have included a few more fan favorites, and have also created my own Mystic Martial Art: Bursting Fist Style, which uses <i>Demolition Training</i> as its initiatory style. I know that Forceful and Precise Martial Arts will serve as the prerequisite for many Mystic styles, but I figured having a few styles require stuff like Verbal Sparring or Free Running could be fun.<br /> <br /> What I wanted to ask about is Emerald Gyre of Aeons Style. Its the 3e Sidereal Style all about manipulating time, whether that be repeating it, accelerating it or reversing it. That's typically not something which Essence can do (the prohibition against time travel being notable), so my initial explanation was that, based on the whole deal with &quot;unwinding,&quot; that the stylist would be using Essence to create and manipulate Aether. Sort of like how Quantakinetics can manipulate Quantum Energies using Noetic Energy.<br /> <br /> However, upon further reflection, I realized that might not be logistically possible, what with how much of a unique phenomena Aether was. So, how would I explain this capacity to manipulate time? Would any of the following work?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>My initial explanation, that EGoA creates and manipulates Aether to manipulate time and possibility.</li> <li>As a substitute for the above, EGoA instead manipulates Flux to do all of the above.</li> <li>Remove the restriction on time control for Essence, and instead make it a rare phenomena on a large scale.</li> </ol>Let me know what you all think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T03:42:07-07:00","id":1511436,"title":"","content":"I was thinking for a while now that Essence should be <i>like</i> Aether, in that it's <i>based on </i>Flux. It's still its own thing, just like Aether is; but it also bears a striking number of conceptual similarities to Flux. I'd go so far as to say that it's Creation's closest analog to Flux; so origins of Essence that involve it leaking into the TC from Creation would, IMHO, make a great deal of sense of the imported Essence ended up bonding with TC Flux.<br /> <br /> That's why most of Essence's manifestations are Skill-based or Attribute-based, just like Aptitude Gifts are Skill-based or Attribute-based. Indeed, there's a lot of overlap between Aptitude Gifts and low-level Essence Charms. Stunts in <b>Exalted</b> are conceptually similar to Dramatic Editing in <b>Trinity Continuum</b>; and in fact, <b>Assassins</b> has an \u201cAlternative Costs for Flashbacks\u201d option (Flashbacks being how it implements Dramatic Editing) that includes <i>Rolled Flashbacks</i> (p.103): instead of paying for the Dramatic Editing with Inspiration or Momentum, you make an appropriate Attribute+Skill roll and pay for the Flashback with successes. In other words, you handle Dramatic Editing as a Stunt rather than as an expenditure of Inspiration. (I'll have to check if the <b>Trinity Continuum Player's Guide </b>has anything like that in it; I don't recall at the moment if it does.)<br /> <br /> In other words, Essence users should have access to Dramatic Editing; and doing so in a Stunt-based manner (similar to <b>Scion</b>'s Twists of Fate) seems very appropriate.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Fate: what is Fate but a manipulation of the timeline? That is, after all, the basis for the Luck Gifts that Talents have. With the Sidereals and Getimians being all about manipulating Fate, I would have no problem with their particular brands of Essence being able to manipulate Time; it's just that, like Talents, most such manipulations tend to be subtle and indirect. EGoA is unusually direct and overt in its manipulation of Time; but it fits the premise.<br /> <br /> Likewise with Prophetic Sorcery. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-12-2023, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T05:14:51-07:00","id":1511440,"title":"","content":"I like the first option. The Emerald would specially fit Aether, for the color.<br /> <br /> Aether is a thing of it\u2019s time, but can also be produced in small scale, what would fit well for a martial art dealing with time in small scale (the surroundings for the duration of the fight).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T06:06:00-07:00","id":1511442,"title":"","content":"Ugh. I edited <i>one word</i> in my last response (\u201cis\u201d to \u201cof\u201d), and the whole thing got unapproved. No matter; I've revised my thoughts on the matter a bit. <br /> <br /> To answer your question in a nutshell, I suppose my answer would be a variation in the third option: as I see it, Essence is Flux-adjacent: like Flux, it operates mostly on a paradigm of Aptitude (Attributes and Skills); and especially where the Sidereals are concerned, it also deals with Fate.<br /> <br /> And what is Fate, of not manipulation of the timeline? (See Luck Gifts.) Given that, I have no problem with saying that Essence can affect time; especially Essence as it's used by Sidereals. <br /> <br /> I would say that Essence comes in three primary flavors: Heavenly Essence (which is used by Solars and Infernals to perform Miraculous Sorcery), Earthly Essence (which is used by Abyssals to perform Necromancy), and Fate (which is used by Sidereals to perform Astrology). I'd allow Sidereals, and possibly other Exalts, to access a variation of Dramatic Editing that gets paid for by Stunt successes rather than by Essence/Inspiration/Momentum: a dice roll incorporating the Exalt's favored Skills or Attributes (as appropriate) can use additional successes to buy a Dramatic Edit instead of picking up Enhancements. This is similar to one of the options provided in <b>Assassins</b>, but also to the way Twists of Fate work in <b>Scion</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T09:10:58-07:00","id":1511454,"title":"","content":"I do have plans to allow Sidereals and Getimians access to Dramatic Editing, albeit through charms rather than natural ability. I also agree that Sidereal/Getimian Essence would be of a markedly different category compared to Solars or Abyssals, just not as huge a degree that I would specifically notate it outside of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I am wavering between first and third, just because I have mechanics created for time and everything. So with Emerald Gyre, Exalted have access to time control, but prolonged use causes damage to the local Essence Density (causing it to lower by 1 level temporarily, and sometimes permanently with exceptionally prolific use.) The reason why is because Creation isn't meant to have rampant distortion of the time stream, due to the Shinma and the foundation of it's making. So, time stuff, Aether or not, causes problems. This way, no matter what option I go with, it's still going to be something you are cautious when using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T18:34:23-07:00","id":1511837,"title":"","content":"Alright, quick little update. I forgot that disease rules were given in Aeon, so I'm going to have to do some rewrites of stuff like Citrine Poxes to fall more in line with the established material.<br /> <br /> Besides that, I had another idea yesterday that I wanted to write out: Wyld Corruption.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wyld Corruption</span><br /> <br /> Wyld Corruption is the phenomena by which stable reality is broken down by the churning primordial chaos that is the Wyld. Much like the &quot;Quantum&quot; Corruption found in TC: Aeon, Wyld Corruption causes a number of issues for those living within its boundaries. Unlike Quantum Corruption however, Wyld Corruption's harmful effects are more <i>prolific</i> than entropic: Both Wyld and Quantum Corruption can cause mutations, but Quantum Corruption does so by distorting the body's safety regulations, causing a massive loss in fertility, body stability and eventually sanity. Wyld Corruption instead fills the body and mind to the point of bursting, causing mutations to bleed out like water. As such, the problem with Wyld Corruption is not a loss in creating life, but rather the capacity to create too much of it, allowing for strange occurrences to happen to children born within the Wyld's domain.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Wyld Corruption is simulated much like Quantum Corruption. It starts at 0, and at 1 point the land becomes a Bordermarche. It increases to a Middlemarche at 4 points, and the Deep Wyld at 7, before emerging into Pure Chaos at 10+. At each stage past Bordermarche, the Difficulty of all actions taken by non-Wyld inhabitants increases (+1 at Middle, +3 at Deep, +5 at Chaos) due to the shifting terrain and dazzling sights creating immense confusion. The Lunar Exalted with their tattoos are immune to this increase in difficulty, as are all other Exalted who use the right Charms.<br /> <br /> Raksha do not use Wyld Corruption as their Power Stat, but do add the increase in Difficulty it provides to their Essence for the purposes of Dice Rolls and other calculations. Thus, the deeper into the Wyld they go, the stronger they become. The reverse is also true, which is part of the reason why the Raksha enjoy those pockets of the Wyld that exist within Creation's borders. Outside of the Wyld, they must spend a Mote each day, which they cannot regain naturally, or suffer a Persistent Injury.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Wyld is composed of, and thrives on, Essence. Without enough Essence to go around, it cannot maintain its chaotic nature. Outside of Creation and other High-Density regions, the Wyld can only go up to 5 points of Corruption in Medium-Density locations, and cannot manifest at all in Low-Density locations. While humanity on Earth has yet to encounter the Fair Folk (in the modern era, that is), once they do they will likely take note that the powers of the Novas, the psychic abilities of the Psions or even the strange narrative-bending luck of the Talents help push these soulless caricatures back to the chaos they thrive in. <hr /><br /> Besides Wyld Corruption, I'm also taking a break from the Martial Arts and Universal Charms to work on some Exalt-specific stuff, starting with the Solars and then the Sidereals. And with the Solars and these new Wyld mechanics, I of course need to bring in the elephant in the room<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Wyld-Shaping Technique (Immortal)</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Requires:</b> Enigmas 4</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spend 3 Motes. The Solar gains access to a new Complex Action, \u201cShape Wyld.\u201d This action requires 1 hour between milestones. Every milestone after the first increases the Difficulty by 1. In addition, for every milestone after the first, roll the area\u2019s starting Wyld Corruption. For every success, generate a Complication for the milestone that, if not bought off, creates a hostile encounter with the inhabitants of the Wyld. Shape Wyld can only be used in areas where the Wyld Corruption exceeds 6 points (aka \u201cDeep Wyld\u201d or greater). This Wyld corruption still exists within the items or places created, it has simply been \u201ctamed\u201d for the Solar\u2019s use. The only way to truly remove it is through Charms such as Wyld-Binding Prana. Possible actions include:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Land (1+):</b> The Solar shapes the Wyld into non-descript land, out to (Essence) Miles by the 1st Milestone, (Essence x 10) Miles by the 2nd Milestone, and multiplied by 10 for every Milestone afterwards. The shaped land is still noticeably tainted, just less so than it was before: It loses (Essence/2) points of Corruption, to a minimum of 4. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Before creating materials, at least 1 Milestone of Land must be generated to provide the basis for the items.</u></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Wealth (1+; at least 2 total):</b> The Solar creates enough riches to constitute a lifetime\u2019s worth of income for a character with a Wealth rating of (Successful Milestones). They gain access to that Edge while the wealth persists, however it is cursed with freaky fortune. Every time it is used, the Storyguide rolls the Edge Dots as dice. For every success, a new Complication is created for the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>next</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> roll the Solar or their team performs using the Wealth. A roll that suffers this complication will not require rolling the Edge Dots to create a new one.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Magical Materials (1+; at least 2 total):</b> The Solar creates enough of a magical material to serve as the necessary resources for a Rank (Milestones + 2) Artifact. These materials, while potent, are generally tainted and must be spiritually cleansed through a ritual or a Charm\u2019s effect to work properly. This constitutes an additional Milestone for the Artifact creation action. Failure to do so creates a new Flaw of up to (Milestones) dots which inhibits its function.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Artifacts (2+; at least 3 total):</b> The Solar creates an Artifact with a Rank equal to (Milestones - 1). This Artifact can be of any material or shape, so long as it does not exceed (Number of Milestones for Land) Size Scale. This Artifact is guaranteed to have a Flaw with a number of dots equal to (Rank, max 5), which provides no benefit.</span></span></li> </ul>\u200bLet me know what you think. Wyld-Shaping Technique here isn't supposed to be a miracle solution, just a quick and dirty way to get what you want if you're willing to risk the side effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T10:07:06-07:00","id":1513301,"title":"","content":"So, status update: I'm currently working on the Sidereal Charms, and I am realizing that I have probably created way too many charms for them (80+ for about half of the abilities, which is obviously a considerable amount). This will need some cutting down, so, if we equate Charms to Gifts, what would you say is a good amount to have per Skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T18:07:28-07:00","id":1517183,"title":"","content":"Critian, I did a big update in Fists of Flux, if you have time download it and check how much of it can be used in your project.<br /> <br /> I mean, you made a huge effort there, but it\u2019s just a suggestion on how to deal with martial arts and maybe some charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/